		"meta": {
			"author": "Stefan Mazur",
			"category": "source",
			"deploymentTarget": {
				"branch": "",
				"name": "Wire",
				"version": {
					"major": 7,
					"minor": 23,
					"patch": 0
				}
			},
			"description": "Rolling Landscape - Art Deco night skyline of the 1930s as parallax silhouettes, with lit windows, stars, a moon, searchlights and airships. Follows the surface model: height is the reference, width shows more or less scene, nothing is stretched. 'Scale' multiplies all sizes, distances and speeds: 1 for any single screen, 1\/3 for three stacked to keep element sizes and show more sky. Nothing moves by itself: drive 'Clock' from Arena (Timeline or BPM Sync; play it backwards to scroll the other way). In Loop mode the city jumps when the timeline restarts. Physics: 'Parallax' sets how much slower the back layers move (0 = all equal, negative = back layers faster), 'Airship Dir' Left \/ Right \/ Random per row, 'Star Scroll' Off = stars fixed, On = stars scroll behind Layer 1. Skyline: 'Layer Count' 0-6 adds layers from back to front; fractional values fade the next layer in. 'Density': share of filled plots. 'Horizon': distance of the base line above the bottom edge. 'Seed': a different value gives a different city, sky and traffic. 'Layer 1-6 Color': one color per layer (1 = back). 'Window Lights': share of lit windows, 'Window Color' for all. Sky: 'Moon X' \/ 'Moon Y' relative to the frame (-1 \/ 1 = edges; the moon sits behind the skyline, so raising Moon Y gives a moonrise), 'Moon Opacity', 'Moon Size' (0 hides it), 'Moon Phase' (0 = new, 0.25 = first quarter, 0.5 = full, 0.75 = last quarter), 'Moon Ray Length' (0 = no rays), 'Moon Color', 'Star Density' (share of possible stars), 'Star Size' (0 hides them), 'Star Color'. Stars keep their position, so density and size can follow FFT. Searchlights: 'Beam Density' 0-1 (share of ground spots with a light; beams sweep with Clock), 'Beam Length', 'Beam Color'. Airships: 'Airship Density' 0-1 (rows over the whole sky, drifting with Clock), 'Airship Color'. Backdrop: 'Backdrop On' colored sky or transparent, 'Backdrop Color'. Drawn by the ISF shader Resource\/RollingLandscape.fs.",
			"displayName": "Rolling Landscape",
			"identifier": "3473280c-9853-4744-8083-c8dbbaba536b",
			"licenseName": "Unlicense",
			"mail": "S.Mazur@cati-co.de",
